# synthetic-turn-removed.jsonl — HAND-WRITTEN, not a wire capture.
#
# No real capture retracts a *middle* turn out of a three-turn session and
# then updates the last turn afterwards: `transcript-wire.jsonl` retracts the
# most recent turn, which never exercises `reindex` remapping a cached slot
# across a shift. This file is written by hand to the shapes in
# `fixtures/msp/msp-ts/msp.d.ts` to pin finding `client-adapter-1`: after
# `turn/retracted` removes the middle turn (`t-syn-2`, a user turn plus its
# assistant turn — two entries in the transcript), the cached slot for the
# last turn's agent-message item must still point at the right turn when its
# revision-2 update lands, not at whatever turn now sits at its old raw
# index.
#
# The `synthetic-` prefix is load-bearing: nothing here was ever on a wire.
